@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Resonance - Docker deployment
skinparam shadowing false
node "Local installation" {
  artifact ".env\nDiscord token and test guild ID" as env
  folder "Host music directory\nMUSIC_DIRECTORY" as music
  database "Named volume\nresonance-data" as data
  node "Docker Compose: bot\nPython 3.12, unprivileged app user" {
    component "bot.main\nResonanceBot + /ping" as bot
    component "discord.py[voice]" as discord
    component "FFmpeg + libopus\ninstalled for future playback" as audio
    folder "/music (read-only)" as mount
    folder "/app/data (writable)" as storage
  }
}
cloud "Discord" as platform
actor "Discord user" as user
user --> platform : /ping
platform <--> discord : HTTPS / Gateway WebSocket\nvoice UDP when implemented
bot --> discord
music --> mount : bind mount
storage --> data : persistent volume
env --> bot : environment variables
note bottom of storage
Reserved for database and derived indexes.
Current bot does not persist data or scan /music.
No SQLCipher integration exists yet.
end note
note bottom of audio
No host audio device or published ports required.
Playback commands are not implemented yet.
end note
@enduml
